      "side": 1,
      "message": "The upstream patch is already in stable in linux-5.10.y branch, and was queued to android12-5.10-lts (see dd887f83ea54), but it broke the build due to some android changes that were never upstreamed (see 705a3e5b1852), so the fix was reverted (see eaa4878a26e1). I went beyond that and checked what that new support does and how to adapt the fix so that it works as in mainline. So I BACKPORTed the fix. I saw that ext4_check_dir_entry() has a new parameter named \"lblk\" and that the author of the patch passed value zero for lblk where ext4_check_dir_entry() was called before his commit. I did the same, I backported the fix and passed zero value for lblk when calling ext4_check_dir_entry(). I described in fewer words what I did in the commit message, above my S-o-b tag, in the [ta: bla bla] section.",
